{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Base directory for this skill: /Users/klopezva/.claude/skills/audio-explainer\n\n# Audio Explainer\n\nThe user wants to *listen* to an explanation (gym, driving, etc.). You write the\nscript; the `audioexplain` CLI turns it into a neural-voice MP3 and prints the\npath. The tool does NOT summarize or call an LLM — that part is your job.\n\n## Steps\n1. Figure out what to explain (\"lo último que hice\", \"el día de trabajo\", a file,\n   a diff, a concept). Gather the context yourself.\n2. Write an **audio-first script** (contract below).\n3. Pick a style: monologue (default) or two-voice podcast (`--style dialogue`).\n4. Synthesize INTO the workspace so the user can find it (he's in VS Code —\n   /tmp files are hard to locate). Use `--out-dir deliverables`:\n   ```bash\n   printf '%s' \"$SCRIPT\" | audioexplain --title \"<short title>\" --out-dir deliverables\n   # from a file:   audioexplain --input script.md --title \"<short title>\" --out-dir deliverables\n   # two voices:     audioexplain --style dialogue --input script.md --title \"...\" --out-dir deliverables\n   # english:        add --english\n   # private/offline: add --provider say\n   ```\n5. **ALWAYS report the ABSOLUTE MP3 path** the tool prints (its `SAVED\n   (absolute):` line / final stdout line), e.g.\n   `/Users/.../deliverables/<file>.mp3`, plus a clickable link and the duration.\n   Also report the generated browser player path:\n   `/Users/.../deliverables/<file>.player.html`. The player has play/pause,\n   `-15/-10/-5/+5/+10/+15` second jumps, common speed presets, progress, and a\n   transcript link. The user keeps losing files — never report only a relative\n   or /tmp path.\n\nIf `audioexplain` is missing, run `audioexplain --doctor`, or install with\n`uv tool install .` from the AudioExplainer repo.\n\n## Browser player\n\n`audioexplain` writes `<file>.player.html` beside every MP3. Use it when the user\nwants to pause, seek, or change speed. VS Code, Finder, Claude app, and normal\nbrowsers can open the HTML directly. If the current browser surface blocks\n`file://`, serve the output folder and open the localhost URL:\n\n```bash\ncd deliverables\npython3 -m http.server 8765 --bind 127.0.0.1\n```\n\nThen open `http://127.0.0.1:8765/<file>.player.html`.\n\n## Audio-first script contract\n\nWhen the user asks for audio, write the script for the **ear**, not the screen:\n\n- Short sentences, active voice, conversational tone.\n- **Never read raw code, file paths, or long URLs aloud** — summarize what the\n  code *does*.\n- Expand acronyms on first use.\n- Punctuation is the only prosody (no SSML): `...` for a pause, `--` for emphasis.\n\nStructure (~5 min default): a spoken **hook/intro** → **2–3 takeaways** (one tight\nparagraph each) → a quick **recap/sign-off**.\n\nTwo-voice podcast (`--style dialogue`): emit speaker-tagged lines, turns under\n~40–50 words. First distinct speaker → voice A, second → voice B.\n\n```\nHost: Hola Kristian. Hoy revisamos el último commit del scanner.\nGuest: Exacto. El cambio clave arregló el límite de peticiones a la API.\nHost: ¿Y por qué importaba?\nGuest: Porque sin eso, el scanner se quedaba a medias en días de mucho volumen.\n```\n\nPrivacy: default `--provider auto` uses neural edge voices for normal content and\nfalls back to offline `say` on sensitive/no-network content (edge-tts sends text\nto Microsoft). Use `--provider say` for clearly private/proprietary material.\n\n(Full contract also in `audio-first-contract.md` next to this file.)\n\n\nARGUMENTS: Resumen en español de la ronda correctiva T-012c del carril fable: qué se buscó (URLs públicas de la interacción real, no portadas), qué se encontró por sistema (9 sistemas) y el hallazgo transversal (nadie enseña la interacción del alumno sin login)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2c729f27-c1ad-49ef-a452-0b34c59ddecf","uuid":"2f42013b-7c5e-4ea9-8508-32f2a3bf9fb2","timestamp":"2026-08-11T03:14:26.307Z","isSynthetic":true}
